# Project Report

> *A comprehensive summary of the Microsoft Sentinel Security Operations Center (SOC) implementation, highlighting the architecture, deployment process, threat detection workflow, and key outcomes.*

---

# Executive Summary

This project demonstrates the deployment of a Microsoft Sentinel Security Operations Center (SOC) using Azure Log Analytics and custom SSH authentication logs. The environment was configured to ingest security telemetry, perform threat hunting with Kusto Query Language (KQL), develop detection logic, investigate suspicious activity, and operationalize detections using Analytics Rules.

The project follows a realistic SOC workflow and showcases the practical application of Microsoft Sentinel for security monitoring and incident detection.

---

# Project Objectives

The primary objectives of this project were to:

- Deploy Microsoft Sentinel in Azure
- Configure a Log Analytics Workspace
- Ingest custom SSH authentication logs
- Perform threat hunting using KQL
- Detect brute-force attacks
- Investigate suspicious source IP addresses
- Create a Scheduled Analytics Rule
- Document the complete engineering workflow

